    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0531" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–2748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-27">October 27,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received October 27—3:03 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>305. Local press reports faculties of Nankai and Peiyang Universities will
                    suspend class work for 3 days as “protest against present state of unbearable
                    living”.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 549, repeated Department 305, Shanghai 517 and Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
